    <main id="main-content" class="site-main">
      <section class="section section--hero hero case-hero case-hero--humans" aria-labelledby="humans-title" data-hero-debug="off">
        <div class="case-hero__panel case-hero__media-panel">
          <div class="case-hero__media humans-media humans-media--hero">
            {% progressiveImage "/assets/figma/Humans/hero.png", "Humans hero mockup placeholder", 1464, 1228, "", "", "", "async", "high" %}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case-hero__panel case-hero__text-panel">
          <div class="case-hero__grid">
            <h1 id="humans-title" class="type-display-2xl case-hero__title">
              <span>Humans.</span>
              <span class="case-hero__title-muted">A brighter layer for daily life</span>
            </h1>
          </div>

          <div class="case-hero__grid">
            <div class="type-heading-lg case-hero__summary">
              <p>Humans is a mobile operator, banking service and marketplace brought together in one digital product. I worked on a new product concept across the mobile app and website, and also designed a set of category icons to help the system feel clearer, more recognisable and more alive.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-content-shell" aria-label="Case content">
        <div class="case-content">
          <section class="case-text-block" aria-label="Humans overview">
            <div class="type-body-lg case-prose">
              <p>Humans combines several daily services in one ecosystem: mobile connection, banking tools and a marketplace. This makes the product useful, but also complex. Every part has its own logic, rhythm and expectations, from checking a mobile balance to browsing offers or managing money.</p>
              <p>The task was to create a new concept for how this product could look and feel across its main surfaces: the mobile application, the website and a set of category icons.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

